hadiths[5]{hadithnumber,text}:
"24013","Narrated to us Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi, narrated to us Zuhayr, from Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Halhalah, from Nuaym ibn Abdullah, from Abu Tikhfah al-Ghifari, he said: My father informed me that he was a guest of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with a group. He said: So we spent the night with him, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out in the night looking about, and he saw him lying flat on his face, so he kicked him with his foot and woke him and said: This is the lying of the people of the Fire."
"24014","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Salamah, from Ibn Ishaq, from Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Ata, from Yaish ibn Tikhfah al-Ghifari, from his father, he said: I was a guest of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) among the poor who were his guests. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out in the night checking on his guest, and he saw me lying flat on my belly, so he kicked me with his foot and said: Do not lie in this lying, for it is a lying that Allah, Mighty and Majestic, hates."
"24015","Narrated to us Yazid, informed to us Ibn Abi Dhib, from al-Harith ibn Abd al-Rahman, he said: While I was sitting with Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, there came upon us a man of Banu Ghifar, a son of Abdullah ibn Tikhfah. So Abu Salamah said: Will you not inform us of the report of your father? He said: My father Abdullah ibn Tikhfah narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when guests were many with him, would say: Let every man go back with his guest. Until one night many guests gathered with him, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let every man go back with his companion. He said: So I was among those who went back with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). When he entered he said: O Aishah, is there anything? She said: Yes, a small Huwaysah I had prepared for your breakfast. He said: So she brought it in a small bowl of hers, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took a little of it and ate it, then he said: Take, in the name of Allah. So we ate of it until we would not look at it. Then he said: Do you have any drink? She said: Yes, a small Lubaynah I had prepared for you. He said: Bring it. So she brought it, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took it and raised it to his mouth and drank a little, then he said: Drink, in the name of Allah. So we drank until, by Allah, we would not look at it. Then we went out and came to the mosque, and I lay down on my face. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out waking the people for prayer: prayer, prayer. And when he went out he would wake the people for prayer. So he passed by me while I was on my face and said: Who is this? I said: I am Abdullah ibn Tikhfah. He said: This is a lying that Allah, Mighty and Majestic, dislikes."
"24016","Narrated to us Ismail ibn Ibrahim, from Hisham al-Dastuwai, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Yaish ibn Tikhfah al-Ghifari, he said: My father was among the people of al-Suffah. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded concerning them, and a man would go back with one man and two men, until I remained fifth of five. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Go. So we went with him to the house of Aishah, and he said: O Aishah, feed us. So she brought Hashishah and we ate, then she brought Haysah like a Qatah bird and we ate, then he said: O Aishah, give us drink. So she brought a large bowl and we drank, then she brought a small cup in which was milk and we drank. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If you wish, spend the night, and if you wish, go to the mosque. We said: Rather we will go to the mosque. He said: While I was in the mosque lying on my belly, a man moved me with his foot and said: This is a lying that Allah hates. So I looked, and it was the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"24017","Narrated to us Hashim, meaning Ibn al-Qasim, narrated to us Abu Muawiyah, meaning Shayban, from Yahya, meaning Ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, he said: Yaish ibn Qays ibn Tikhfah informed me, from his father, and his father was among the people of al-Suffah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O so-and-so, go with this one with you. And he mentioned its meaning."
